course: dictionary
lesson: 12434
title: Deceleration: slowing down
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Deceleration is the word for slowing down. When something's speed gets smaller, it is decelerating. «The cyclist felt a strong deceleration when she squeezed the brakes.»
explain: Acceleration is the opposite: it means speeding up. A ball rolling across the grass slows to a stop because friction pushes against it, so the ball decelerates. A skydiver's parachute opens, and she decelerates quickly.
explain: Scientists measure deceleration in metres per second per second, written m/s². The number tells you how much the speed drops every second.
fact: Deceleration means slowing down.
fact: Deceleration is the opposite of acceleration.
fact: Friction and air resistance can cause deceleration.
fact: Deceleration is measured in metres per second per second (m/s²).
fact: Seatbelts help protect you during sudden deceleration in a crash.
exercise: «The car's brakes caused a fast deceleration as it came to a stop.» What is deceleration? | Going backwards | *Slowing down | Turning left | Speeding up
exercise: A ball rolls across the grass and slows to a stop because of friction. What is this slowing called? | Acceleration | *Deceleration | Gravity | Magnetism
exercise: Which unit is used to measure deceleration? | Degrees Celsius | *Metres per second per second | Litres | Kilograms
test: «Acceleration is speeding up, and deceleration is the opposite.» Which word means speeding up? | Friction | Deceleration | Stopping | *Acceleration
test: Why do seatbelts help during sudden deceleration in a crash? | They warm the seats | They make the car go faster | They make the car lighter | *They hold your body back as the car suddenly slows
exam: «A skydiver's parachute opens and she decelerates quickly.» What does decelerates mean? | Turns around | Stays at the same speed | Falls faster | *Slows down
